facts:
**Translation** slides a shape: right/left and up/down, with no turning or flipping.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.6,0)--(1.6,0.7)--(0.7,0.7)--(0.7,1.8)--(0,1.8)--cycle;
\draw (2.8,0.9)--(4.4,0.9)--(4.4,1.6)--(3.5,1.6)--(3.5,2.7)--(2.8,2.7)--cycle;
\draw[->, dashed] (0,0)--(2.8,0.9);
\node[below, font=\small] at (0.8,0) {object};
\node[below, font=\small] at (3.6,0.9) {image};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Reflection** flips a shape over a mirror line; the image is back-to-front.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.6,0)--(1.6,0.7)--(0.7,0.7)--(0.7,1.8)--(0,1.8)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (2.6,-0.5)--(2.6,2.6);
\draw (5.2,0)--(3.6,0)--(3.6,0.7)--(4.5,0.7)--(4.5,1.8)--(5.2,1.8)--cycle;
\node[below, font=\small] at (0.8,0) {object};
\node[below, font=\small] at (4.4,0) {image};
\node[above, font=\small] at (2.6,2.6) {mirror line};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Rotation** turns a shape about a point by an amount such as a quarter ($90^{\circ}$) or half ($180^{\circ}$) turn.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes, calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (V) at (2.4,0.8);
\coordinate (W) at (-0.8,2.4);
\draw (0.8,0.8)--(2.4,0.8)--(2.4,1.5)--(1.5,1.5)--(1.5,2.6)--(0.8,2.6)--cycle;
\draw (-0.8,0.8)--(-0.8,2.4)--(-1.5,2.4)--(-1.5,1.5)--(-2.6,1.5)--(-2.6,0.8)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (O)--($(O)!1.15!(V)$);
\draw[dashed] (O)--($(O)!1.15!(W)$);
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.9cm] {angle=V--O--W};
\fill (O) circle (2pt);
\node[below, font=\small] at (0,-0.05) {$O$};
\node[right, font=\small] at (2.5,2.2) {object};
\node[left, font=\small] at (-2.7,2.2) {image};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

