development.question_text:
Describe fully how shape $A$ moves to shape $B$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,4);
\draw (0.3,2.3)--(1.7,2.3)--(1.7,3.3)--(0.8,2.8)--cycle;
\draw (4.3,0.3)--(5.7,0.3)--(5.7,1.3)--(4.8,0.8)--cycle;
\node[above] at (1,3.3) {$A$};
\node[above] at (5,1.3) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Describe fully how the shaded triangle moves to its image.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (-3,-1) grid (3,3);
\draw[dashed] (0,-1.4)--(0,3.4);
\draw[fill=gray!25] (-2.7,-0.7)--(-0.7,-0.7)--(-2.7,2.3)--cycle;
\draw (2.7,-0.7)--(0.7,-0.7)--(2.7,2.3)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Describe fully how arrow $A$ moves to arrow $B$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[->] (0.6,0.5)--(2.4,0.5);
\draw[->] (0.5,-0.6)--(0.5,-2.4);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[above] at (1.5,0.5) {$A$};
\node[right] at (0.5,-1.5) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Describe fully how arrow $M$ moves to arrow $N$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\draw[->] (-0.6,0.7)--(-2.3,1.5);
\draw[->] (0.6,-0.7)--(2.3,-1.5);
\fill (C) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (-1.5,1.2) {$M$};
\node[below] at (1.5,-1.2) {$N$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

